vement and Regulation) (Northern Ireland) Order 2003, and providers are inspected against the Department of Health minimum care standards for the setting type. Adult safeguarding operates under the regional adult safeguarding partnership policy. Certain events are notifiable to RQIA, and RIDDOR still applies UK-wide to the HSE for work-related incidents. Always work from the current published standards and regulations.</p><h2>How quickler runs it</h2><p>Quickler turns a recurring audit or a whole quality theme into a workflow that runs over the WhatsApp Business API. The registered manager or a nominated staff member walks the home and answers each prompt in their existing WhatsApp chat, with text, a voice note or a photo tied to the standard it evidences. Voice notes are transcribed automatically. The report and improvement plan generate themselves, and a provider running several registered homes sees each one's position on a single dashboard.</p><h2>Pricing</h2><p>Pricing is only for active users: [[price:bundles]]. An active user is someone who completed at least two workflows that month, so you can add every manager, nurse, care worker and bank worker across the provider and pay only for who actually files something. The free tier is 20 reports a month and up to 10 photos per report, no card and no trial clock.</p><h2>What quickler is not</h2><p>Quickler is not a care record, care management, eMAR or clinical system, and holds no resident care data. It captures the audit walk and the evidence around it: photos of the setting, observations against the standards, the state of records at the point of check. For medication and care plans it records that the check was done and captures the evidence, without copying a resident's personal or clinical data into quickler. Care plans, medication administration records and personal care logs stay in your care planning system, which remains the single source of truth. Quickler is the audit and evidence layer that sits alongside the care system.</p><p>Quickler is not affiliated with or endorsed by RQIA, and whether your evidence satisfies an inspection is a judgement for you and your inspector. This page is general information, not regulatory advice; always work from the current published minimum care standards and regulations.</p><h2>Related guides</h2><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-software-uk.html\">Care home compliance software UK</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-home-compliance-software-scotland.html\">Care home compliance software Scotland</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/care-inspectorate-wales-compliance-software.html\">Care Inspectorate Wales compliance software</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/hiqa-compliance-software-ireland.html\">HIQA compliance software Ireland</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/five-regulators-one-job-british-isles.html\">Five regulators, one job</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/medication-storage-audit-care-uk.html\">Medication storage audit</a></li></ul>",
